  "description": "Filler alloy joining methods where the base metal does not melt. Brazing uses filler metals melting above 450°C (brass, silver alloys) for structural joints. Soft soldering uses low-melting alloys (tin-lead, tin-silver) below 450°C for electrical connections, plumbing, and sheet metal seams.",
